class Solution {
    public int minimumBoxes(int[] apple, int[] capacity) {
        int tot=0;
        for(int i=0;i<apple.length;i++) tot+=apple[i];
        Arrays.sort(capacity);
        int count=0;
        int sorted=0;
        for(int i=capacity.length-1;i>=0;i--){
            sorted+=capacity[i];
            count++;
            if(sorted>=tot){
                return count;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}

Explanation:
First, calculate the total number of apples needed to store.
Sort the capacity array so we can use the largest boxes first.
Start picking boxes from the end of the sorted array and keep adding their capacities.
Count how many boxes are used until the total capacity becomes greater than or equal to total apples.
